#! rate=44118 block=128 tracks=4
# 03 Notes, gates and note-offs (R3 c, R4 a-b, R10).
# A chord's gates expire together and leave in swap_remove order; a
# same-pitch note on the next step retriggers after its own off; mute flushes
# the track's gates at once; a track stopped at the bar has its gate flushed
# by service_tick before step_tick runs; Stop flushes every open gate.
# D1 trace: no D2-D7 behaviour is involved, so the FM-1 default mode should
# produce <stem>.d1.jsonl: the same events, each tick at its own frame.
@0 tog 0 0 60 100 64 90 67 80
@0 tog 0 1 60 100
@0 tog 0 4 48 100
@0 slen 0 4 4 48 200
@0 tog 1 0 36 127
@0 slen 1 0 0 36 300
@0 tog 1 8 38 110
@0 tog 2 2 72 100
@0 slen 2 2 2 72 380
@0 play
# pos 48: track 1's long 36 is sounding
@11136 mute 1 1
@23040 mute 1 0
@45000 stoptrk 2
# pos 390: the second pass's chord and 36 are open
@89700 stop
